TARGET BENEFICIARIES

Rural schools in desert villages will use it for food preservation. Small farms in oasis communities will use it for produce storage. Disaster relief operations in refugee camps located in arid zones will use it for emergency food supplies.

EXPECTED OUTCOMES
Continuous refrigeration will provide 24 hours per day, 7 days per week operation in desert conditions. food preservation will maintain 99 percent viability of stored food. Diesel elimination will result in 100 percent renewable energy consumption. Early warning will provide alerts before battery failure occurs. Scalability will allow replication of this system in any desert region worldwide.





